<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eureka Rebellion</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1854">1854</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Eureka Stockade</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Eureka Rebellion was a revolt by gold miners at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ballarat">Ballarat</a> in Victoria in 1854 against the costly miners' licences and the conduct of the authorities. Led by Peter Lalor, the miners built a stockade and raised the Southern Cross flag, but soldiers and police stormed it on 3 December 1854, killing about 22 miners. Public sympathy led to the acquittal of the rebels, the abolition of the licence and a wider vote in Victoria.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/eureka-rebellion.jpg" alt="Eureka Rebellion" width="320" height="235" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: John Black Henderson (1827-1918) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Eureka_stockade_battle.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
